# POC2 multi-agent SDD + TDD

Hub: `.docs/plans/planning.spec.MD` §6.3 · `D17`. Template: `.docs/specs/_template.spec.ts`.

POC-1 (`poc/`) is **frozen**. Do not edit it. Do not open tasks against it.

## Agents (disjoint ownership)

| Agent | Spec sections | Code | Forbidden |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Orchestrator** | header, §1 Scope, §8 Requires, §9 sign-off | `poc2/todo.md` checkoff, refuse open `requires` | numbers, THREE, tests |
| **Programming / Three.js** | §2 Contract, §3 Fields, §5 Rules, §6 View | classes, `extends THREE.*`, `dispose()`, pools | BALANCE values, skipping tests |
| **Game Design** | §4 BALANCE / feel / leveling / graphics | `BALANCE` numbers, palette, cadence | class shape, tests, literals outside BALANCE |
| **TDD** | §7 cases | `{subject}.test.ts` written **red** first; runs `npm run test` | production implementation |

## Order on every card

1. Orchestrator copies the template and fills Scope + Requires.
2. Programming fills contract / memory / view.
3. Game Design fills BALANCE + feel + leveling + graphics.
4. TDD names cases and writes the failing test file.
5. Programming implements until green. TDD re-runs `verify`. Game Design play-checks. Orchestrator ticks DoD.

A spec with an empty agent section is incomplete. `N/A` is allowed; blank is not.

## Implementation gates

- Spec before code. Tests before implementation.
- `interface` + `class`, one public class per `kebab-case.ts`.
- `update(dt)` = logic; `syncRender()` = transforms/opacity/material only.
- Gameplay numbers only in `BALANCE` (`RUL-12`). Gamepad indices, deadzone, trigger threshold and haptic presets live in `BALANCE.controls.gamepad` and `BALANCE.haptics` (`D18`). No third-party pad library.
- Zero per-frame allocation on hot paths.
- `npm run verify` in `poc2/` must be green before Orchestrator marks done.
